# Ocentra Parent Protocol Boundary Rules

Product parent UI communicates through HostBridge into Rust-owned parent runtime
contracts. Dev web and Rust-owned LAN/runtime transports may still use endpoint
or WebSocket envelopes, but WebSocket is not the product `TSX UI <-> parent
Rust` path.

Do not treat any HostBridge, endpoint, or WebSocket payload as ad hoc JSON.

## Protocol Change Order

1. Define the canonical product DTO, action, route snapshot, or event shape in
   `crates/schema`, `crates/parent-runtime-core`, or the owning Rust
   domain/runtime crate.
2. Add or update Rust serialization, round-trip, and encoded-shape tests.
3. Generate or expose TypeScript bridge DTOs for UI consumers.
4. Use Effect Schema only at untrusted TypeScript edges or generated validation
   edges.
5. Wire Rust runtime/service dispatch.
6. Wire `apps/portal` through HostBridge or DevWebHostBridge as presentation.
7. Run focused contract, Rust, bridge, integration, and UI smoke tests.

## Message Rules

- Every command and event has a stable domain-owned type.
- Every payload has a schema, even when currently empty.
- Every field name comes from the Rust-owned schema/protocol owner.
- Version protocol shapes before changing existing semantics.
- Prefer additive events over changing historical event meaning.

## Bidirectional Assumption

Design Rust-owned communication for two-way product and runtime flows:

- TSX UI asks Rust parent runtime for route snapshots through HostBridge
- Rust parent runtime dispatches actions into event bus/domain code
- child/runtime agents report observations through Rust-owned transport
- future remote parent surfaces address multiple devices through Rust-owned
  route/session/read-model boundaries

Do not hard-code a single-device future into protocol names.

## Local Routes Are Still Boundaries

The portal is not trusted just because it runs on localhost or the same LAN.
Parse every inbound action/command and reject unknown event/command types.

Protocol routes must distinguish HostBridge, dev loopback, LAN, and future cloud
relay paths. Do not overload `localhost` for cross-device LAN access.
